<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>@ViewData["Title"] — Data Annotations Demo</title>
    <style>
        body { font-family: sans-serif; max-width: 640px; margin: 2rem auto; padding: 0 1rem; }
        .field-validation-error { color: #c00; font-size: 0.875rem; display: block; margin-top: 2px; }
        .validation-summary-errors { color: #c00; background: #fee; border: 1px solid #c00; padding: 0.5rem 1rem; border-radius: 4px; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
        .validation-summary-errors ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.25rem; }
        .form-group { margin-bottom: 1rem; }
        label { display: block; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 0.25rem; }
        input[type="text"], input[type="email"], input[type="password"],
        input[type="tel"], input[type="url"], input[type="number"],
        input[type="date"] { width: 100%; padding: 0.375rem 0.5rem; box-sizing: border-box; border: 1px solid #aaa; border-radius: 3px; }
        input.input-validation-error { border-color: #c00; }
        button[type="submit"] { padding: 0.5rem 1.5rem; background: #0066cc; color: white; border: none; border-radius: 3px; cursor: pointer; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <main>
        @RenderBody()
    </main>

    @*
        CLIENT-SIDE UNOBTRUSIVE VALIDATION — PREVIEW (→ 14. Client-Side Validation)
        ============================================================================
        The three scripts below enable jQuery Validate + jquery.validate.unobtrusive,
        which is the ASP.NET Core MVC client-side validation stack.

        HOW IT WORKS (brief overview):
          1. Razor Tag Helpers (asp-validation-for, asp-for) emit data-val-* attributes
             on <input> and <span> elements based on the model's DataAnnotations.
          2. jquery.validate reads those data-val-* attributes and wires up validation
             rules that run in the browser WITHOUT a server round-trip.
          3. jquery.validate.unobtrusive bridges ASP.NET Core's naming convention
             (data-val-required, data-val-length, data-val-regex, etc.) to jQuery
             Validate's rule API.

        ATTRIBUTE → data-val-* MAPPING EXAMPLES:
          [Required]              → data-val-required="..."
          [StringLength(20)]      → data-val-maxlength="..."  data-val-minlength="..."
          [Range(1, 100)]         → data-val-range="..."
          [RegularExpression]     → data-val-regex="..."
          [EmailAddress]          → data-val-email="..."
          [Compare("Password")]   → data-val-equalto="..."
          [CreditCard]            → data-val-creditcard="..."

        CLIENT-SIDE DOES NOT REPLACE SERVER-SIDE:
          JavaScript can be disabled. Always validate on the server (ModelState.IsValid).
          Client-side is an enhancement, not a replacement.

        IN PRODUCTION: host these scripts locally (wwwroot/lib/) via LibMan or npm
        rather than loading them from a CDN on every page load.
        COVERED IN DETAIL LATER → 14. Client-Side Validation
    *@
    <script src="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/jquery/3.7.1/jquery.min.js"></script>
    <script src="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/jquery-validate/1.19.5/jquery.validate.min.js"></script>
    <script src="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/jquery-validation-unobtrusive/4.0.0/jquery.validate.unobtrusive.min.js"></script>

    @await RenderSectionAsync("Scripts", required: false)
</body>
</html>
